findings:
[{'explanation': 'Austria intends to maintain an average annual photovoltaic capacity expansion of 2 GW up to 2040, with a scenario target of PV supplying 20% of total energy supply and an overall technical PV potential of 41 TWh annual generation by 2040; these figures are based on assessments in the Integrated Austrian Network Infrastructure Plan (ÖNIP/NIP) and are reported as scenarios or planned targets. [Data: Entities 156, 175, 152, 164, 9, 160; Relationships 175, 201, 167, 9, 188]', 'summary': 'Austria has scenario-based and planned targets for significant PV expansion by 2040.'}
