 {'explanation': "The Renewables Acceleration Areas zoning instrument is planned/required by the EU's RED III directive, which mandates Member States to designate specific zones for speedier renewable installations such as photovoltaics; this requirement is reflected in Austrian policy planning. [Data: Entities 249, 248, 267; Relationships 298, 297, 327]", 'summary': 'EU and national policy instruments aim to facilitate acceleration of renewables, particularly PV.'}
