    "summary": "The supplied graph records describe interconnected Austrian and EU policy targets, national subsidy mechanisms, regulatory obligations, economic considerations, and technical scenarios for photovoltaic (PV) market development up to 2040. Key entities are the Renewable Expansion Act (EAG) and related Austrian legal and policy targets, which establish a 100% nationally balanced renewable electricity goal by 2030 and specify at least 11 TWh additional PV generation by that year. Financial support for PV expansion includes investment subsidies for Agri-PV, premiums for innovative installations, deductions for ground-mounted PV, and proposals for cumulative support combining PV with green roofs. Economic viability and constant incentives are cited as scenario-based prerequisites for achieving the anticipated annual expansion of approximately 2 GW, aimed to potentially reach a 41 TWh PV generation potential by 2040. There are also EU directives prescribing PV obligations for building construction and renovation. The documentation makes explicit use of qualifying language (e.g., scenario, planned action, under discussion) and reveals limitations, such as non-finalized obligations for parking lots, scenario-dependent targets, and the absence of real-world implementation data.",
    "findings": [
        {
            "summary": "Austria’s legal framework (EAG) establishes official PV expansion and renewable electricity consumption targets for 2030.",
            "explanation": "The Erneuerbaren-Ausbau-Gesetz (EAG) sets the national target of 100% balance-sheet renewable electricity consumption by 2030 and codifies a minimum of 11 TWh additional PV generation by 2030, as evidenced by the existence of both the entity and explicit relationship records linking legal acts with defined targets. [Data: Entities 10, 8, 44, 159; Relationships 8, 38, 36]"
        },
        {
            "summary": "Multiple financial instruments and support schemes facilitate different forms of PV installations.",
            "explanation": "Investment subsidies support Agri-PV, premiums are allocated to innovative PV system types, and deductions apply to open-space PV; proposals exist for cumulative support combining PV and green roofs, with some measures established, others proposed or scenario-based. [Data: Entities 151, 215, 216, 232, 218, 233, 234, 214; Relationships 166, 251, 252, 277, 278, 279, 250]"
        },
        {
            "summary": "Economic viability and ongoing incentives are identified as scenario-based constraints for sustained annual PV expansion.",
            "explanation": "A scenario/planned expansion of approximately 2 GW PV capacity per year is said to depend on continued incentives and the economic viability of PV system operations, with the market premium cited as a prerequisite for economic success and operator financing until at least 2040. [Data: Entities 329, 327, 318, 319, 345, 346; Relationships 392, 391, 393, 420, 417]"
        },
        {
            "summary": "Regulatory frameworks and obligations aim to mobilize built-up or sealed surfaces and newly constructed or renovated buildings for PV deployment.",
            "explanation": "Regulatory incentives and obligations, some legally in force (e.g., housing law amendment for row houses), some under proposal or discussion (e.g., mandatory PV for large parking lots), and EU directives for new or renovated buildings, collectively aim to increase PV coverage via specific building types and land uses. [Data: Entities 208, 212, 217, 221, 229, 244, 231; Relationships 243, 244, 245, 255, 256, 273, 276, 289]"
        },
        {
            "summary": "PV ground-mounted installations may include biodiversity-enhancing features to align with EU renaturation goals.",
            "explanation": "Records state that biodiversity-oriented PV ground-mount designs can contribute to EU biodiversity restoration targets, and that financial support/deductions may be linked to such system types. [Data: Entities 220, 235, 228; Relationships 262, 263, 272]"
        },
        {
            "summary": "Targets and scenarios for cumulative PV generation by 2040 depend on maintaining current market and policy instruments.",
            "explanation": "Planned or scenario targets indicate a cumulative PV generation potential of up to 41 TWh by 2040 if supportive instruments and economic preconditions remain in place, without asserting that these targets are guaranteed outcomes. [Data: Entities 330, 329, 318, 346; Relationships 401, 392, 417]"
        }
    ],
    "rating": 9.0,
    "rating_explanation": "The report covers highly interlinked policy targets, regulatory and financial support mechanisms, economic conditions, and expansion scenarios that collectively represent major pillars of Austria’s solar-market development according to the supplied graph records."
}

