    "summary": "This community centers on photovoltaics (PV) as a core technology and policy focus within Austria’s electricity supply transformation and climate objectives. Relationships are established between PV and a range of energy sectors (heating, industry, mobility), stakeholders (businesses, citizens), and infrastructure elements (public grids, storage). Numerous policy, regulatory, and quality assurance schemes (such as the Eco-design Directive and transparent quality labels) explicitly support PV deployment, while identified constraints include grid connection, market capacity, economic viability, regulatory barriers, and societal acceptance. Dynamic tariffs, storage, and sector coupling (including e-mobility and heat pumps) are discussed as synergistic measures. Visible limitations include the lack of quantified numeric targets, measured outcomes, and unresolved challenges such as low or negative electricity prices during periods of high PV generation. The records are extensive in their associative and aspirational linkages while often lacking operational or performance data.",
